{%- comment -%}
  How many 30-day supplies each delivery of a selling plan holds: 1 for every
  30 days, 2 for 60, 3 for 90, so the shopper never runs out. Read from
  Recharge's "Order Frequency and Unit" option ("60-day"), at least 1, and 1
  when the plan doesn't say. The Liquid twin of supplyUnits in
  packages/shopify/src/subscribe-and-save.ts.

  Outputs a number; capture it, then `| plus: 0`.

  Accepts:
  - selling_plan: {Object} the plan (allocation.selling_plan)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign units = 1
  for option in selling_plan.options
    if option.name contains 'requency'
      assign parts = option.value | downcase | split: '-'
      assign count = parts[0] | plus: 0
      assign unit = parts[1] | strip
      assign days = count
      if unit contains 'week'
        assign days = count | times: 7
      elsif unit contains 'month'
        assign days = count | times: 30
      endif
      assign units = days | divided_by: 30.0 | round
      if units < 1
        assign units = 1
      endif
    endif
  endfor
  echo units
-%}
